## Overnight Oats & Chia Puddings (Make-Ahead Magic)

These creamy, dreamy breakfasts come together in minutes the night before—and taste like dessert when you wake up.

### 1. High-Protein Peanut Butter & Chocolate Chia Pudding

Chia seeds create a thick, creamy texture while delivering **fiber and healthy omega-3 fatty acids**. Peanut butter adds flavor and plant-based protein, balanced by deep cocoa notes.

### 2. High-Protein Apple & Peanut Butter Overnight Oats

Creamy peanut butter and Greek-style yogurt add plenty of protein, while chopped apples bring natural sweetness and crunch. Rolled oats soak up all the flavors overnight.

### 3. Peaches & Cream Overnight Oats

Sweet ripe peaches combined with creamy oats. The oats soften overnight in the fridge, resulting in a thick, pudding-like texture without any cooking.

### 4. Lemon "Custard" Overnight Oats

Creamy vanilla and apple oats layered with a smooth and tangy lemon and turmeric chia "custard." This breakfast tastes just like dessert but leaves you feeling full of energy. _Fiber: 11.6g per serving_

### 5. Pumpkin Pie Overnight Oats

Packed with **16 grams of fiber and zero added sugar**. Made with old-fashioned oats, chia seeds, and pumpkin puree.

### 6. Coconut-Mango Turmeric Chia Pudding

A tropical-inspired layered breakfast with a creamy coconut base and a mango-date puree for naturally sweet, fiber-rich goodness.

### 7. High-Protein Blueberry & Peanut Butter Chia Pudding

Chia seeds soak up a dreamy blend of almond milk and blueberries, delivering a perfect make-ahead breakfast packed with fiber and protein.

### 8. High-Protein Mango & Tahini Overnight Oats

Rolled oats soak overnight in a mixture of protein-rich Greek yogurt, coconut milk, and tahini, creating a thick and satisfying texture with juicy mango chunks.

### 9. Chocolate Teff Porridge

A creamy, high-fiber, calcium-rich, gluten-free breakfast sweetened with dates. Rich, naturally gluten-free, and packed with plant protein.

### 10. Apple Cinnamon Chia Seed Oatmeal

A creamy, high-fiber, make-ahead meal with 32g protein, balanced with magnesium, calcium, and natural sweetness from fresh apples.

### 11. Cinnamon Oatmeal with Fresh Fruit, Almonds, and Chia Seeds

A refreshing vegan oatmeal recipe that's high in fiber and low in added sugar and saturated fat.

