## Hot & Hearty Oatmeal Variations

Oatmeal is a classic for good reason—half a cup of rolled oats provides about **4–5 grams of fiber**. Here's how to level it up:

### 12. Carrot Cake Overnight Oats

Loaded with calcium, protein, fiber, and vitamin A. Chia seeds add heart-healthy soluble fiber and omega-3s.

### 13. Cranberry Almond Oatmeal

Simple but delicious, ready in just 5 minutes. Low in calories and sugar yet **high in fiber (11g per serving)**.

### 14. Banana & Chia Porridge

Cook oats with milk or water, mash in a banana, and stir in chia seeds for a creamy, fiber-packed start.

### 15. High-Protein PB&J Baked Oats

A delicious mash-up that combines the nostalgic flavors of peanut butter and jelly with the hearty texture of baked oats. Packed with protein from peanut butter, Greek-style yogurt, and eggs.

