## Savory High-Fiber Breakfasts

Who says fiber has to be sweet? These savory options are packed with flavor and gut-friendly nutrients.

### 16. Chickpea & Potato Hash

A one-pan breakfast packed with anti-inflammatory ingredients. Spinach, chickpeas, and zucchini add fiber and protein, making this dish filling and balanced. Ready in under 30 minutes.

### 17. Avocado Toast with Burrata

Burrata takes this avocado toast to the next level. Half a medium avocado has nearly **7g of fiber**, and whole-grain toast adds another **2g**.

### 18. Black Bean & Pepper Jack Quiche

A creamy egg filling packed with **fiber-rich black beans**, sweet peppers, and spicy pepper Jack cheese.

### 19. Breakfast Burrito with Beans

With **7 grams of fiber per half-cup**, black beans are a breakfast superstar. Wrap them in a whole-wheat tortilla with eggs and veggies.

### 20. Cauliflower Steaks with Poached Eggs & Pesto Hollandaise

A weekend-worthy dish featuring cauliflower "steaks" flavored with Italian seasoning, topped with sautéed kale and a poached egg.

### 21. Lentil and Veggie Scramble

Lentils pack an incredible fiber punch—pair them with sautéed vegetables and eggs for a savory, satisfying breakfast.

### 22. Chickpea Pancakes

A savory twist on pancakes using chickpea flour, packed with fiber and plant protein.

### 23. Whole Grain Avocado Toast with Egg

Top whole-grain toast with mashed avocado and a poached or fried egg for a perfect balance of fiber, healthy fats, and protein.

### 24. Black Beans, Rice & Fried Egg

An excellent breakfast choice that scores high in protein, fiber, and flavor.

