## Cereals & Toast (Quick & Classic)

Sometimes simple is best—and these classic options deliver serious fiber.

### 32. High-Fiber Cereal (Dietitian-Approved Picks)

Look for cereals with **5 grams or more of fiber per serving**. Top picks include:

- **Fiber One Original:** 27g fiber per cup
- **Kellogg's All-Bran Buds:** 19.5g fiber per ½ cup
- **Cascadian Farm Hearty Morning:** 11g fiber per cup
- **Kashi GO Cinnamon Crunch:** 10g fiber per cup
- **Grape-Nuts:** 7g fiber per ½ cup

### 33. Whole-Grain Toast with Nut Butter and Banana

Swap plain white bread for **100% whole grain or sprouted grain bread (3–5g fiber per slice)**. Top with almond butter and sliced banana.

### 34. Greek Yogurt Parfait with Berries and Flaxseed

Layer Greek yogurt with berries, and stir in a tablespoon of ground flaxseed. Berries like raspberries pack **8g fiber per cup**.

### 35. Cottage Cheese with Pineapple and Flaxseed

Cottage cheese is a dietitian-recommended breakfast staple. Add pineapple and a sprinkle of flaxseed for extra fiber.

